In release (round7.json, l6merge#1: 1.08-1.13 s and 5.3-5.6 s against 1 s and 6 s) the reruns bound again passes it, and the one-selection bound fails it by 8-13%.

So two kinds of regression pass both bounds:
- round six's own, on a machine a quarter faster in debug or a tenth faster in release;
- one half its size, on this machine.
A slower 4-core CI runner likely catches round six on both bounds. The 500-box test's 30 s bound (:1204) is about 300 times its 65-105 ms per case.

